{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539596642,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfe6affeApOQ0VkusgZ7Wu","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e5272b002atORKov9r2mL5h","sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfe6affeApOQ0VkusgZ7Wu","messageID":"msg_1d2e51831001X7BForrcOh3wpp","type":"tool","id":"call_07de259bd0c94724b86f8f5f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-t007-* 2>/dev/null; ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-t007-* 2>/dev/null; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- INSTALL-SKILLED.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"diff --git a/INSTALL-SKILLED.md b/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\nindex a50cadec1e..67190189a8 100644\n--- a/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n+++ b/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@ DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a\n \n Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n \n+To see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n+\n ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n \n Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/INSTALL-SKILLED.md b/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\nindex a50cadec1e..67190189a8 100644\n--- a/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n+++ b/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@ DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a\n \n Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n \n+To see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n+\n ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n \n Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rm -rf \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-t007-* 2>/dev/null; ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-t007-* 2>/dev/null; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539595563,"end":1794539596642}}}}
