{"type":"text","timestamp":1794539608589,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfe6affeApOQ0VkusgZ7Wu","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e549d3002xpqaf9cyFkBPS4","sessionID":"ses_e2d1dfe6affeApOQ0VkusgZ7Wu","messageID":"msg_1d2e53723001oVCRGUcNCA8EUt","type":"text","text":"T007 is done.\n\n**File written**\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` — one paragraph added under `### Check the Install`, directly after the Codex hook-approval paragraph and before `### Meaning Matching for Commands`.\n\n**Verify output**\n- `rg -c \"advisor_recommend --json\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` → `1`\n- The documented command:\n  - Sandboxed run (`SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to a fresh temp dir): `sk-doc`, one line, neither empty nor `null`. Temp dir and any process naming it were cleaned up, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-t007-*` now prints nothing.\n  - Note: a plain run first exited 69 with `@spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale (source content differs from the attested build)`. That is not caused by this task: `git status` shows `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and `.../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` modified by the concurrent wave-1 workers (T003, T005). I did not rebuild `dist` because it is outside this task's file scope. The verified run used the repository's documented dev pass-through, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`, which skips only the freshness attestation. The final T022/T017 rebuild will clear the staleness before the authoritative verification.\n\n**Not done**\n- `tasks.md` checkbox left unticked, as instructed.\n- No other files touched. I did not read the routing corpus, so no holdout row was read or printed.\n\nThe one thing for the coordinator: the wide verification of this documented command against a live build waits on the wave rebuild, since the current `dist` is stale from concurrent source edits.","time":{"start":1794539604435,"end":1794539608589}}}
